content:
Editors and drive apps declare their behaviour by writing into a global config store, and the setters come in two flavours: imperative (`setPH…Config`) and mount-time (`useSetPH…Config`).

Two config slices matter here:

```ts
export type PHAppConfig = {
  /** Empty array means any document type is allowed. */
  allowedDocumentTypes?: string[];
  isDragAndDropEnabled?: boolean;
};

export type PHDocumentEditorConfig = {
  isExternalControlsEnabled?: boolean;
};
```

Both are members of the larger `PHGlobalConfig` intersection, and `setPHAppConfig` / `setPHDocumentEditorConfig` simply iterate the partial's keys and forward each one to the per-key global setter — so setting a slice is exactly equivalent to setting its keys individually.

The wrapper hooks are what codegen actually emits. The app template writes `useSetPHAppConfig(editorConfig)` at the top of the generated editor, with the object living in a sibling `./config.ts`. Read the implementation before relying on it: the hook guards its effect with a one-shot `isInitialized` state flag, so it applies the config **once on mount and never again**. Passing a config object that changes between renders will not update anything — for dynamic changes call the imperative `setPHAppConfig` directly.

**Naming caveat — the academy is stale here.** `04-Reference/05-EditorsUI/01-ReactHooks.md` documents `PHDriveEditorConfig`, `setPHDriveEditorConfig` and `useSetPHDriveEditorConfig`. Those identifiers have **zero occurrences** anywhere in the monorepo outside build output; the slice was renamed to `PHAppConfig` and the functions to `setPHAppConfig` / `useSetPHAppConfig`, consistent with drive editors having been renamed to apps. The `PHDocumentEditorConfig` names in the doc are still correct. Some doc comments in source also lag, describing `setPHAppConfig` as "the global drive config".

_Source: packages/reactor-browser/src/types/config.ts, src/hooks/config/set-config-by-object.ts and packages/codegen/src/templates/app/editor.ts (Powerhouse v6.2.2-dev.45); the academy's React Hooks page still uses the removed setPHDriveEditorConfig names._
